  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Cango has completed a dramatic pivot from Chinese auto finance into Bitcoin mining, emerging as a large-scale, cost-efficient operator. The company is modernizing its fleet, retiring older rigs, and emphasizing energy-efficient production over sheer hashrate expansion. However, the narrative has been upended by the liquidation of almost its entire Bitcoin treasury, which triggered sharp market skepticism and a debate over whether this was strategic deleveraging or panic selling. The subsequent launch of an AI compute platform, EcoHash, adds an unproven revenue dimension, leaving the business story deeply mixed between mining efficiency and a high-risk diversification.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership executed the mining transition with notable operational discipline, rapidly scaling output, cutting mining costs, and delivering a profitability turnaround. Yet that credibility was severely damaged by the abrupt sale of 86% of the company’s Bitcoin holdings and the simultaneous unveiling of an AI pivot. The appointment of a new CFO and the shift in capital allocation signal an aggressive transformation, but the timing—amid a weakened balance sheet and thin margins—has caused confusion. Investors are now questioning whether management possesses a coherent long-term strategy or is chasing narratives at the expense of conviction.",
